Subject: [PATCH 0/2] i2c: qcom-cci: keep the shared CAMNOC clock alive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On sm7125 (Galaxy A52) the CCI I2C controller shares cam_cc_camnoc_axi_clk
with the camera subsystem. When CCI gates that clock while the CAMNOC bus
is unclocked, the branch halt FSM wedges "stuck at on" and later camera
captures return no frames. Fix it by holding a small CAMNOC interconnect
bandwidth vote whenever CCI's clocks are enabled.

Patch 1 documents the new optional interconnects properties; patch 2 adds
the vote in the driver. The interconnect path is optional, so existing
platforms without it are unaffected.

Note: the related system-sleep fix (routing suspend through
pm_runtime_force_suspend/resume) is already present in mainline as of
v7.3-rc5, so only the interconnect work remains.


